<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Choose a set for a difference</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>\(\xi = \{1, 2, \ldots, {@N@}\}\) and \(A = {@dset(A)@}\).</p><p>Write a set \(B\), using elements of \(\xi\) only, so that \(A - B = {@dset(S)@}\) and \(B\) has at least one element that is not in \(A\). Many answers are correct.</p><p>\(B =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>\(A - B\) is \(A\) with every element of \(B\) removed. To leave exactly \({@dset(S)@}\), \(B\) must contain \({@dset(AmS)@}\) (the elements of \(A\) to be removed) and must not contain any element of \({@dset(S)@}\).</p><p>\(B\) also needs an element of \(\xi\) that is not in \(A\), such as \({@x0@}\). For example \(B = {@dset(Bs)@}\) gives \(A - B = {@dset(S)@}\). Any other elements of \(\xi\) outside \(A\) may be added.</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
